1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,935
Complaints are product research if you log them.

2
00:00:02,935 --> 00:00:05,504
This lesson is about improve from refunds/feedback.

3
00:00:05,504 --> 00:00:06,971
Turn complaints into product.

4
00:00:06,971 --> 00:00:09,540
Do not treat this as theory only.

5
00:00:09,540 --> 00:00:13,209
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

6
00:00:13,209 --> 00:00:18,712
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

7
00:00:18,712 --> 00:00:22,748
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

8
00:00:22,748 --> 00:00:26,784
Stay practical: log three improvements before you optimize branding or tools.

9
00:00:27,104 --> 00:00:32,822
Log three improvements from refunds or feedback: what broke, what you will change, by when.

10
00:00:32,822 --> 00:00:35,110
Remember the objective: log three improvements.

11
00:00:35,110 --> 00:00:39,303
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

12
00:00:39,303 --> 00:00:43,878
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

13
00:00:43,878 --> 00:00:48,072
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

14
00:00:48,072 --> 00:00:52,646
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

15
00:00:52,646 --> 00:00:55,315
Talk to a real person when possible.

16
00:00:55,315 --> 00:00:56,840
Feedback beats guessing alone.

17
